age\", None) is not True:\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n            record = copy.copy(record)\n            record.msg = self._truncate(message)\n            record.args = ()\n    msg = super().format(record)\n    ...\n```\n\nWait: `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True` — need exactly True. `1 is True` is False, good. But `getattr(..., None) is not True` works.\n\nHmm, but caution: `record.getMessage()` may raise if args mismatch; then super().format would too. Fine.\n\nAlso careful about float/int check: `isinstance(True, int)` is True so bool must be rejected.\n\nTruncation function:\n```python\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\nhead = (budget - len(marker) + 1) // 2\ntail = budget - len(marker) - head\nreturn message[:head] + marker + (message[-tail:] if tail > 0 else \"\")\n```\nCheck budget 32: marker len 15, remaining 17, head = (17+1)//2 = 9, tail = 17-9=8. ✓\n\nAlso requirement \"消息不超过预算时保持原样\" — <= budget.\n\nAlso the multi-line handling: `if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:` — record.message set by super().format on the copy, so it's the truncated message. Good. But if we truncated the message and the record is a copy, `record.message` after super().format is the truncated message. Fine.\n\nAlso default init: `_setup_logger` should pass `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`. Need import from deepinfer envs — logger.py currently imports os, sys etc. Importing `from deepinfer import envs` in logger.py — check circular import: environ.py imports? Let me check lines 1-30 of environ.py. envs module likely imports os, threading, typing only. logger imports deepinfer.envs — safe probably (stats_logger imports `from deepinfer import envs` and `deepinfer.logger`).\n\nBut careful: importing envs in logger at module import triggers `_setup_logger()` which reads env var — that's fine and desired.\n\nHmm, but risk: environ may import logger? Let me check lines 1-30.\n\nstats_logger: `_log_worker`: `logger.info(m)` -> `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nLet's read environ head now."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 9491, "completion_tokens": 1474, "total_tokens": 10965, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4096}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1383}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4096, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 5395}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
