gger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nAlso ensure default handler not duplicated: existing.\n\nNow I need the exact text for replace edits. environ snippet exact from evidence. logger class exact. stats _log_worker exact.\n\nLet me write edits. For environ, insert helper after _str function and add config in envs. Also maybe documentation string.\n\nNeed to know the rest of envs to place logging section—doesn't matter, insert after \"# -- Runtime --\" block maybe. I'll insert after DEEPINFER_JIT_CACHE_DIR line:\n\n    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(\n        lambda v: None if v is None else _int_min(v, 32)\n    )\n\nHelper defines min check. Let me define:\n\ndef _optional_int_min(v: str | None, minimum: int) -> int | None:\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    value = int(v)\n    if value < minimum:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{value!r} must be >= {minimum}\")\n    return value\n\nUse lambda. Error wrapped with name by descriptor. Good.\n\nNow make edits."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 9496, "completion_tokens": 1694, "total_tokens": 11190, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4096}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1302}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4096, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 5400}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
